{
  "$schema": "https://datapackage.org/profiles/2.0/datapackage.json",
  "name": "gadm-3.6",
  "title": "GADM database of Global Administrative Areas, version 3.6 (all levels, shapefiles; licensed)",
  "description": "GADM version 3.6 (2018), the database of the world's administrative areas, as the official six-layer shapefile delivery gadm36_levels_shp.zip, extracted and unchanged: gadm36_0 (countries) to gadm36_5 (the finest sub-divisions), each as .shp, .shx, .dbf, .prj and .cpg, in EPSG:4326. Level-1 features carry GID_0 (ISO 3166 alpha-3 country code), NAME_0, GID_1 and NAME_1 among their attributes. The RESKit example for northern Germany and the German North Sea reads gadm36_1 to select Schleswig-Holstein, Hamburg, Bremen, Niedersachsen and Mecklenburg-Vorpommern by GID_0 and NAME_1, and to subtract land from the German EEZ.",
  "homepage": "https://gadm.org/",
  "version": "3.6",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "GADM version 3.6 download page (gadm36_levels_shp.zip, \"six separate layers as shapefiles\")",
      "path": "https://gadm.org/download_world36.html"
    },
